(r/'qa/PHASE-REVIEW.md').write_text('''# FX15 nonloop spirit-fire review\n\nThe original runtime strip, atlas04 row3 and higher-resolution peak slot were viewed before authoring. The approved exact order is spirit-onset → spirit-growth → leafy-spirit-peak → spirit-residue. Preserve sage/mint/cream spirit fire, an olive leaf bed, rising leaves and the peak curling branch.\n\n- Onset has a modest wisp, two airborne leaves and pale drawn motes above the low bed.\n- Growth raises and reshapes the wisp, moves loose leaves upward and introduces one internal leaf motif.\n- Peak broadens the plume, adds three internal leaves and a right-side curling olive branch. The low bed remains in the common region.\n- Residue removes the peak branch and internal leaves, narrows and lowers the spirit into a smaller nonempty wisp, and leaves two settling leaves and one mote. There is no renewal or cyclic restart.\n\nThe measured visible spirit tips are source Y 529, 290, 57 and 598. Color-threshold spirit area grows from 92,077 to 154,156 to 235,758 source pixels, then falls to 52,571. These are diagnostics of authored shape changes, not code-applied fading or geometric operations. The mint threshold can include pale leaf highlights and motes, so it is not a literal segmentation of all flame material.\n\nLeaf-bed bottom contacts are source Y 1141, 1165, 1171 and 1172. Total variation is 31 source pixels, or 0.69 logical pixels. The first pair's 24-pixel/0.54-logical-pixel variation was specifically accepted by the parent after native black/white review. Later frames add only 7 source pixels/0.16 logical pixels beyond that. The later frames retain slight changes in drawn leaf outlines and highlights. This is asset-specific visual tolerance, not a general relaxation of registration rules. The lower-region raw silhouette IoU is also recorded, but includes the changing spirit base and fine leaf tips; it is not an independent fixed-bed acceptance gate.\n\nFull-source black/white and six-background native 32/64 composites were inspected. No outside light curtain, backing card, glow cloud, clipping, white fringe or magenta backing was found. Cream/mint interiors remain readable on light and dark backgrounds because the sage edge carries their silhouette. The source perimeter has only alpha-1 samples, conditionally verified by actual composite measurements and inspection. Final logical 2px padding is fully alpha 0.\n\nThis is one pass: four equal 1/12-second samples, APNG num_plays 1, nominal clip 1/3 second. The final wisp remains available as the nonloop terminal sample. No extra hold frame or 420ms removal rule was added; a future consumer owns final display/removal. Parent final quartet static acceptance was received on 2026-10-20 after complete native and terminal comparison. Browser/live playback was not observed, and no current literal consumer was found.\n''')
